{:paths ["src"]
 :deps {io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph
        {:git/sha "5b4e5e70837b849b14b6a5800894e3be202ad5fa"}
        ;; kotoba-lang/labor is this vertical's bespoke domain capability
        ;; library (contracts, timesheets, wages, payroll).
        ;;
        ;; This was a sibling path, on the stated grounds that "labor's own
        ;; deps use sibling paths, so it is not consumable as a git dep".
        ;; Measured 2026-08-17: labor has ZERO :local/root deps -- it takes
        ;; html and css by git sha. The comment was false, and it was the
        ;; reason nobody converted this: a claim about ANOTHER repo, written
        ;; here, that nothing ever rechecked.
        ;;
        ;; The sibling path made this repo's README claim ("forkable by any
        ;; qualified operator") quietly untrue, and made it ungateable on the
        ;; murakumo fleet, which ships one repo's tree and no siblings.
        io.github.kotoba-lang/labor
        {:git/url "https://github.com/kotoba-lang/labor.git"
         :git/sha "febdf680a038995228b7a85838ca3b73b9cada39"}
        ;; the itonami actor pattern's governor layer, written once.
        ;; 90a2944e is the commit that gave scope-owner-mismatch a
        ;; :scope-key, because this actor's contract names ownership
        ;; :contract/employer while the request names it :client-id.
        io.github.kotoba-lang/governor
        {:git/url "https://github.com/kotoba-lang/governor.git"
         :git/sha "90a2944e617e58b9c90314b7e84b003ec3ea0c1f"}
        ;; what a tax record must carry, by jurisdiction. a4a68050 is the
        ;; commit that added the withholding facet, because this actor is the
        ;; first payer-side consumer: 4311 checks the RECEIVING side of
        ;; インボイス制度 and `tehai` the ISSUING side. The 源泉徴収 rule was
        ;; read out of 所得税法 第百八十三条第一項 before it was enforced --
        ;; taxlaw's standing rule -- and it lives there rather than here
        ;; because a second actor will need the same law.
        io.github.kotoba-lang/taxlaw
        {:git/url "https://github.com/kotoba-lang/taxlaw.git"
         :git/sha "a4a68050e30622dd92990dcdab94038a07d46998"}
        ;; the shared langchain.db store seam (EDN-blob codec + identity
        ;; schema + seq-keyed event streams) — ADR-2607141600. What
        ;; `payroll.store`'s DatomicStore is built on; the codec is NOT
        ;; re-hand-rolled here, which is the duplication (the same two-liner
        ;; in ~190 store.cljc files) that library was extracted to end.
        ;;
        ;; Checked by PARSING its deps.edn as EDN at the pin below, not by
        ;; grepping it: that file's comments contain the literal `:local/root`
        ;; while its coordinates contain none, and a grep reports the comment.
        ;; Measured 2026-08-18 — 4 distinct coordinates across :deps and every
        ;; alias's :extra-deps/:replace-deps/:override-deps, 0 `:local/root`;
        ;; same for its own single dependency, langchain-clj @ 51e7b61e
        ;; (6 coordinates, 0 `:local/root`).
        io.github.kotoba-lang/langchain-store
        {:git/url "https://github.com/kotoba-lang/langchain-store.git"
         :git/sha "b986669f72276568c97e1fa5b331a5ff3017bf69"}}

 ;; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
 ;; ZERO `:local/root`, and that is a hard property rather than a preference.
 ;;
 ;; A sibling path makes this repo unforkable (its README claims otherwise) and
 ;; structurally ungateable on the murakumo fleet, which ships ONE repo's tree
 ;; and no siblings — a gate would fail on a missing directory and read as a
 ;; broken build rather than as a broken dependency declaration.
 ;;
 ;; Measured 2026-08-18: the suite was run from a fresh `git clone` into /tmp
 ;; with `GITLIBS` pointed at an empty directory and no sibling checkout of
 ;; langgraph, labor, governor, taxlaw or langchain-store in existence. That is
 ;; the only check that actually proves the property; grepping this file does
 ;; not, because a TRANSITIVE `:local/root` is just as fatal and does not
 ;; appear here.
 ;; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
 :aliases
 {
  ;; clj-kondo from deps (no binary), errors fail CI. Added because this repo
  ;; could not be linted at all -- across this fleet an absent or broken :lint
  ;; alias is what let misplaced docstrings, dead code and even a false-green
  ;; test verdict survive unreported (cloud-itonami-isic-561/563/920).
  :lint {:replace-deps {clj-kondo/clj-kondo {:mvn/version "2024.11.14"}}
         :main-opts    ["-m" "clj-kondo.main"
                        "--lint" "src" "test"
                        "--fail-level" "error"]}
  :test {:extra-paths ["test"]
         :extra-deps {io.github.cognitect-labs/test-runner
                      {:git/tag "v0.5.1" :git/sha "dfb30dd"}}
         :main-opts ["-m" "cognitect.test-runner"]}}}
